      "confidence": 0.85,
      "curator_note": "Alpha (radical-site) cleavage of the O-ionized di-n-hexyl ether molecular ion (di-n-hexyl ether drawn as C6H13-OCH2-C5H11; odd electron on O1). The odd electron on O1 forms the O1=C2 pi bond of the oxocarbenium C6H13-O(+)=CH2 (m/z 115, 3%) while the C2-C3 sigma bond to the pentyl chain cleaves, expelling the n-pentyl radical C5H11. Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: Eq. 8.46 is a branching fragmentation map whose arrows are reaction-pathway arrows labelled 'alpha' and 'i' (with the neutral/radical loss written above each), NOT curved fishhook arrows; all three electron moves are curator-inferred from the printed 'alpha' pathway label. Encoded with the canonical THREE fishhooks: move<1> O1 odd electron into the forming O1-C2 pi bond, move<2> one C2-C3 electron into that same pi bond, move<3> the other C2-C3 electron onto C3 (the departing pentyl radical)."
    },
